CYBRA MODULE 13 — DUAL BACKEND CONSENSUS CONTROLLER
PATCH_ID=CYBRA-M13-PATCH-0001

1. Backend A is independently required.
2. Backend B is independently required.
3. Backend A confirmation MUST be separate from Backend B confirmation.
4. One backend MUST NOT confirm for both backend roles.
5. Backend A MUST provide a state hash.
6. Backend B MUST provide a state hash.
7. Backend A and Backend B state hashes MUST be identical.
8. Backend confirmations MUST reference the exact ORDER_HASH.
9. Backend confirmations MUST reference the exact TERMS_HASH.
10. Backend confirmations MUST reference the exact CHAIN_ID.
11. Backend confirmations MUST reference the exact CONTRACT_ADDRESS.
12. Missing Backend A confirmation means WAITING/BLOCKED.
13. Missing Backend B confirmation means WAITING/BLOCKED.
14. Missing state hash means WAITING/BLOCKED.
15. Different state hashes mean FALSE/RETRY.
16. Different order hashes mean FALSE/RETRY.
17. Different terms hashes mean FALSE/RETRY.
18. Different chain IDs mean FALSE/RETRY.
19. Different contract addresses mean FALSE/RETRY.
20. Matching hashes alone MUST NOT establish GLOBAL_TRUE_100.
21. Backend consensus MUST NOT release escrow.
22. Backend consensus MUST NOT authorize final release.
23. Backend consensus MUST NOT authorize LIVE.
24. Backend consensus MUST NOT send a blockchain transaction.
25. Backend A MUST NOT manufacture Backend B evidence.
26. Backend B MUST NOT manufacture Backend A evidence.
27. TEST evidence MUST NOT automatically become LIVE evidence.
28. Evidence corrections MUST create a new PATCH_ID.
29. Frozen snapshots MUST NOT be silently modified.
30. The controller reports consensus only for its own module.
31. GLOBAL_TRUE_100 remains controlled by the complete CYBRA state machine.
